    {"id":"h1t","type":"text","x":-490,"y":-986,"width":680,"height":25,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a2","roundness":null,"seed":603,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"locked":false,"text":"THE REPLICATION LAG PROBLEM","rawText":"THE REPLICATION LAG PROBLEM","fontSize":22,"fontFamily":8,"textAlign":"center","verticalAlign":"middle","containerId":"h1r","originalText":"THE REPLICATION LAG PROBLEM","autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25},
    {"id":"lag_exp","type":"text","x":-490,"y":-942,"width":680,"height":75,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#e03131","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a3","roundness":null,"seed":604,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"locked":false,"text":"Async replication means followers are BEHIND the leader.\nThis lag = a window of time where followers have stale data.\nUsually milliseconds. Under load: seconds. This causes weird bugs users notice.","rawText":"Async replication means followers are BEHIND the leader.\nThis lag = a window of time where followers have stale data.\nUsually milliseconds. Under load: seconds. This causes weird bugs users notice.","fontSize":20,"fontFamily":8,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"originalText":"Async replication means followers are BEHIND the leader.\nThis lag = a window of time where followers have stale data.\nUsually milliseconds. Under load: seconds. This causes weird bugs users notice.","autoResize":false,"lineHeight":1.25},
    {"id":"h2r","type":"rectangle","x":-500,"y":-848,"width":700,"height":45,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"#a5d8ff","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a4","roundness":{"type":3},"seed":605,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[{"type":"text","id":"h2t"}],"updated":1,"locked":false},
    {"id":"h2t","type":"text","x":-490,"y":-836,"width":680,"height":25,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a5","roundness":null,"seed":606,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"locked":false,"text":"GUARANTEE 1 — READ-YOUR-OWN-WRITES","rawText":"GUARANTEE 1 — READ-YOUR-OWN-WRITES","fontSize":22,"fontFamily":8,"textAlign":"center","verticalAlign":"middle","containerId":"h2r","originalText":"GUARANTEE 1 — READ-YOUR-OWN-WRITES","autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25},
    {"id":"ryw_exp","type":"text","x":-490,"y":-792,"width":680,"height":125,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a6","roundness":null,"seed":607,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"locked":false,"text":"Problem:\n  User updates their profile photo → written to leader.\n  User refreshes page → read goes to follower → sees OLD photo. Confusing!\n  User thinks their update was lost.\n\nSolution — Read-your-writes consistency:\n  After a user writes, reads for THAT user always go to the leader (or a replica\n  that's confirmed it received the write).\n  Everyone else can still read from followers.\n\nHow to implement:\n  Option A: User reads their own data → always go to leader. (Works, but wastes followers)\n  Option B: Track last-write timestamp per user. Read from a follower only if it has\n  caught up past that timestamp. Otherwise go to leader.\n  Option C: Route user to same replica always (sticky sessions / consistent hashing).","rawText":"Problem:\n  User updates their profile photo → written to leader.\n  User refreshes page → read goes to follower → sees OLD photo. Confusing!\n  User thinks their update was lost.\n\nSolution — Read-your-writes consistency:\n  After a user writes, reads for THAT user always go to the leader (or a replica\n  that's confirmed it received the write).\n  Everyone else can still read from followers.\n\nHow to implement:\n  Option A: User reads their own data → always go to leader. (Works, but wastes followers)\n  Option B: Track last-write timestamp per user. Read from a follower only if it has\n  caught up past that timestamp. Otherwise go to leader.\n  Option C: Route user to same replica always (sticky sessions / consistent hashing).","fontSize":20,"fontFamily":8,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"originalText":"Problem:\n  User updates their profile photo → written to leader.\n  User refreshes page → read goes to follower → sees OLD photo. Confusing!\n  User thinks their update was lost.\n\nSolution — Read-your-writes consistency:\n  After a user writes, reads for THAT user always go to the leader (or a replica\n  that's confirmed it received the write).\n  Everyone else can still read from followers.\n\nHow to implement:\n  Option A: User reads their own data → always go to leader. (Works, but wastes followers)\n  Option B: Track last-write timestamp per user. Read from a follower only if it has\n  caught up past that timestamp. Otherwise go to leader.\n  Option C: Route user to same replica always (sticky sessions / consistent hashing).","autoResize":false,"lineHeight":1.25},
    {"id":"h3r","type":"rectangle","x":-500,"y":-640,"width":700,"height":45,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"#a5d8ff","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a7","roundness":{"type":3},"seed":608,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[{"type":"text","id":"h3t"}],"updated":1,"locked":false},
    {"id":"h3t","type":"text","x":-490,"y":-628,"width":680,"height":25,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a8","roundness":null,"seed":609,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"locked":false,"text":"GUARANTEE 2 — MONOTONIC READS","rawText":"GUARANTEE 2 — MONOTONIC READS","fontSize":22,"fontFamily":8,"textAlign":"center","verticalAlign":"middle","containerId":"h3r","originalText":"GUARANTEE 2 — MONOTONIC READS","autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25},
    {"id":"mr_exp","type":"text","x":-490,"y":-584,"width":680,"height":125,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a9","roundness":null,"seed":610,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"locked":false,"text":"Problem:\n  User reads a comment → goes to Follower A (lag 1s) → sees it.\n  User refreshes → goes to Follower B (lag 5s) → comment is GONE.\n  User is confused: did I imagine it? It looks like time travel backward.\n\nSolution — Monotonic reads:\n  Guarantee: once you've seen data at a point in time, you will never see\n  an older version. Reads never go backward.\n\nHow to implement:\n  Each user always reads from the SAME replica.\n  Use consistent hashing on user ID → always maps to same follower.\n  If that follower dies → rehash to a different one.","rawText":"Problem:\n  User reads a comment → goes to Follower A (lag 1s) → sees it.\n  User refreshes → goes to Follower B (lag 5s) → comment is GONE.\n  User is confused: did I imagine it? It looks like time travel backward.\n\nSolution — Monotonic reads:\n  Guarantee: once you've seen data at a point in time, you will never see\n  an older version. Reads never go backward.\n\nHow to implement:\n  Each user always reads from the SAME replica.\n  Use consistent hashing on user ID → always maps to same follower.\n  If that follower dies → rehash to a different one.","fontSize":20,"fontFamily":8,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"originalText":"Problem:\n  User reads a comment → goes to Follower A (lag 1s) → sees it.\n  User refreshes → goes to Follower B (lag 5s) → comment is GONE.\n  User is confused: did I imagine it? It looks like time travel backward.\n\nSolution — Monotonic reads:\n  Guarantee: once you've seen data at a point in time, you will never see\n  an older version. Reads never go backward.\n\nHow to implement:\n  Each user always reads from the SAME replica.\n  Use consistent hashing on user ID → always maps to same follower.\n  If that follower dies → rehash to a different one.","autoResize":false,"lineHeight":1.25},
    {"id":"h4r","type":"rectangle","x":-500,"y":-430,"width":700,"height":45,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"#a5d8ff","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a10","roundness":{"type":3},"seed":611,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[{"type":"text","id":"h4t"}],"updated":1,"locked":false},
    {"id":"h4t","type":"text","x":-490,"y":-418,"width":680,"height":25,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a11","roundness":null,"seed":612,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"locked":false,"text":"GUARANTEE 3 — CONSISTENT PREFIX READS","rawText":"GUARANTEE 3 — CONSISTENT PREFIX READS","fontSize":22,"fontFamily":8,"textAlign":"center","verticalAlign":"middle","containerId":"h4r","originalText":"GUARANTEE 3 — CONSISTENT PREFIX READS","autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25},
    {"id":"cpr_exp","type":"text","x":-490,"y":-374,"width":680,"height":150,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a12","roundness":null,"seed":613,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"locked":false,"text":"Problem: You read a REPLY before you read the original QUESTION.\n  User A posts: 'How is the weather?'\n  User B posts: 'It is very cold!'\n  Follower A gets A's message (small lag). Follower B is way behind.\n  You read from both followers → you see 'It is very cold!' first with no context.\n  Looks like B is talking to nobody. Causality is broken.\n\nSolution — Consistent prefix reads:\n  Guarantee: if you write A then B, anyone who reads B must also see A first.\n  Writes that are causally related must be read in order.\n\nHow to implement:\n  Option A: Write all causally related writes to the same partition (shard).\n  Then reads within a partition always come in order.\n  Option B: Track causal dependencies with version vectors — read only from\n  replicas that have processed all dependencies of the data you need.","rawText":"Problem: You read a REPLY before you read the original QUESTION.\n  User A posts: 'How is the weather?'\n  User B posts: 'It is very cold!'\n  Follower A gets A's message (small lag). Follower B is way behind.\n  You read from both followers → you see 'It is very cold!' first with no context.\n  Looks like B is talking to nobody. Causality is broken.\n\nSolution — Consistent prefix reads:\n  Guarantee: if you write A then B, anyone who reads B must also see A first.\n  Writes that are causally related must be read in order.\n\nHow to implement:\n  Option A: Write all causally related writes to the same partition (shard).\n  Then reads within a partition always come in order.\n  Option B: Track causal dependencies with version vectors — read only from\n  replicas that have processed all dependencies of the data you need.","fontSize":20,"fontFamily":8,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"originalText":"Problem: You read a REPLY before you read the original QUESTION.\n  User A posts: 'How is the weather?'\n  User B posts: 'It is very cold!'\n  Follower A gets A's message (small lag). Follower B is way behind.\n  You read from both followers → you see 'It is very cold!' first with no context.\n  Looks like B is talking to nobody. Causality is broken.\n\nSolution — Consistent prefix reads:\n  Guarantee: if you write A then B, anyone who reads B must also see A first.\n  Writes that are causally related must be read in order.\n\nHow to implement:\n  Option A: Write all causally related writes to the same partition (shard).\n  Then reads within a partition always come in order.\n  Option B: Track causal dependencies with version vectors — read only from\n  replicas that have processed all dependencies of the data you need.","autoResize":false,"lineHeight":1.25},
    {"id":"summary_box","type":"rectangle","x":-500,"y":-200,"width":700,"height":120,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1971c2","backgroundColor":"#e7f5ff","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a13","roundness":{"type":3},"seed":614,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[{"type":"text","id":"sum_t"}],"updated":1,"locked":false},
    {"id":"sum_t","type":"text","x":-488,"y":-188,"width":676,"height":100,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1971c2","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a14","roundness":null,"seed":615,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"locked":false,"text":"The 3 Consistency Guarantees — Quick Reference:\n  Read-your-writes    → You always see your own updates. (user-level guarantee)\n  Monotonic reads     → Reads never go backward in time. (no disappearing data)\n  Consistent prefix   → Causally related writes arrive in order. (no seeing reply before question)\n\nAll 3 are weaker than full strong consistency (linearizability).\nThey are practical, implementable, and sufficient for most applications.\nNone of them require synchronous replication — they just require smart routing.","rawText":"The 3 Consistency Guarantees — Quick Reference:\n  Read-your-writes    → You always see your own updates. (user-level guarantee)\n  Monotonic reads     → Reads never go backward in time. (no disappearing data)\n  Consistent prefix   → Causally related writes arrive in order. (no seeing reply before question)\n\nAll 3 are weaker than full strong consistency (linearizability).\nThey are practical, implementable, and sufficient for most applications.\nNone of them require synchronous replication — they just require smart routing.","fontSize":20,"fontFamily":8,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":"summary_box","originalText":"The 3 Consistency Guarantees — Quick Reference:\n  Read-your-writes    → You always see your own updates. (user-level guarantee)\n  Monotonic reads     → Reads never go backward in time. (no disappearing data)\n  Consistent prefix   → Causally related writes arrive in order. (no seeing reply before question)\n\nAll 3 are weaker than full strong consistency (linearizability).\nThey are practical, implementable, and sufficient for most applications.\nNone of them require synchronous replication — they just require smart routing.","autoResize":false,"lineHeight":1.25}
  ],
